{"1-5":{"people":[{"id":"herod-g2264i","name":"Herod","kind":"person","brief":"A Tetrarch","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"james-g2385g","name":"James","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"john-g2491h","name":"John","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":2,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":3}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G5438","lemma":"φυλακή","tr":"phulakē","gloss":"prison","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"G1577","lemma":"ἐκκλησία","tr":"ekklēsia","gloss":"assembly","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":114},{"base":"G4074","lemma":"Πέτρος","tr":"Petros","gloss":"Peter","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":155},{"base":"G1619","lemma":"ἐκτενῶς","tr":"ektenōs","gloss":"fervently","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G0701","lemma":"ἀρεστός","tr":"arestos","gloss":"pleasing","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2559","lemma":"κακόω","tr":"kakoō","gloss":"to harm","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"G0106","lemma":"ἄζυμος","tr":"azumos","gloss":"unleavened","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"G4084","lemma":"πιάζω","tr":"piazō","gloss":"to arrest","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"G4815","lemma":"συλλαμβάνω","tr":"sullambanō","gloss":"to seize","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"G1911","lemma":"ἐπιβάλλω","tr":"epiballō","gloss":"to put on","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":18}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"MAT","chapter":24,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"Then they will deliver you over to be persecuted and killed, and you will be hated by all nations because of My name.","from":1},{"book":"1CO","chapter":12,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"If one part suffers, every part suffers with it; if one part is honored, every part rejoices with it.","from":5},{"book":"JAS","chapter":5,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"Therefore confess your sins to each other and pray for each other so that you may be healed. The prayer of a righteous man has great power to prevail.","from":5},{"book":"JHN","chapter":15,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Remember the word that I spoke to you: ‘No servant is greater than his master.’ If they persecuted Me, they will persecute you as well; if they kept My word, they will keep yours as well.","from":1},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"Pray in the Spirit at all times, with every kind of prayer and petition. To this end, stay alert with all perseverance in your prayers for all the saints.","from":5},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"for which I am an ambassador in chains. Pray that I may proclaim it fearlessly, as I should.","from":5},{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Pray without ceasing.","from":5},{"book":"MAT","chapter":10,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"But beware of men, for they will hand you over to their councils and flog you in their synagogues.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":3},{"id":"bethany-and-friends","title":"Bethany and the Women Around Jesus","people":3},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"the-twelve","title":"The Twelve Apostles","people":3},{"id":"john-baptist-circle","title":"John the Baptist's Circle","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2}]},"6-11":{"people":[{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":3,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"herod-g2264i","name":"Herod","kind":"person","brief":"A Tetrarch","count":2,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G0032","lemma":"ἄγγελος","tr":"angelos","gloss":"angel","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":175},{"base":"G4074","lemma":"Πέτρος","tr":"Petros","gloss":"Peter","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":155},{"base":"G0254","lemma":"ἅλυσις","tr":"halusis","gloss":"chain","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"G2264","lemma":"Ἡρώδης","tr":"Hērōdēs","gloss":"Herod","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"G5438","lemma":"φυλακή","tr":"phulakē","gloss":"prison","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"G0190","lemma":"ἀκολουθέω","tr":"akoloutheō","gloss":"to follow","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":90},{"base":"G1417","lemma":"δύο","tr":"duo","gloss":"two","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":134},{"base":"G5495","lemma":"χείρ","tr":"cheir","gloss":"hand","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":175},{"base":"G1831","lemma":"ἐξέρχομαι","tr":"exerchomai","gloss":"to go out","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":216},{"base":"G0844","lemma":"αὐτόματος","tr":"automatos","gloss":"by itself","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"But during the night an angel of the Lord opened the doors of the jail and brought them out, saying,","from":7},{"book":"ACT","chapter":16,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"Suddenly a strong earthquake shook the foundations of the prison. At once all the doors flew open and everyoneʼs chains came loose.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":105,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"They bruised his feet with shackles and placed his neck in irons,","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":105,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"The king sent and released him; the ruler of peoples set him free.","from":7},{"book":"DAN","chapter":6,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"My God sent His angel and shut the mouths of the lions. They have not hurt me, for I was found innocent in His sight, and I have done no wrong against you, O king.”","from":11},{"book":"PSA","chapter":146,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"He executes justice for the oppressed and gives food to the hungry. The LORD sets the prisoners free,","from":7},{"book":"DAN","chapter":3,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Nebuchadnezzar declared, “Blessed be the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, who has sent His angel and delivered His servants who trusted in Him. They violated the kingʼs command and risked their lives rather than serve or worship any god except their own God.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":19,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"At daybreak the angels hurried Lot along, saying, “Get up! Take your wife and your two daughters who are here, or you will be swept away in the punishment of the city.”","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2}]},"12-17":{"people":[{"id":"husband-of-mary-g3137n","name":"husband of Mary","kind":"person","brief":"Husband of Mary","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"mark-g3138","name":"Mark","kind":"person","brief":"Paul's companian","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"mary-g3137l","name":"Mary","kind":"person","brief":"Barnabus' relative","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":3,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"rhoda-g4498","name":"Rhoda","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"james-g2385i","name":"James","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":17}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G4440","lemma":"πυλών","tr":"pulōn","gloss":"gate","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":18},{"base":"G4074","lemma":"Πέτρος","tr":"Petros","gloss":"Peter","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":155},{"base":"G2925","lemma":"κρούω","tr":"krouō","gloss":"to knock","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"G0518","lemma":"ἀπαγγέλλω","tr":"apangellō","gloss":"to announce","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"G0455","lemma":"ἀνοίγω","tr":"anoigō","gloss":"to open","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":77},{"base":"G5037","lemma":"τε","tr":"te","gloss":"and","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":215},{"base":"G1340","lemma":"διϊσχυρίζομαι","tr":"diischurizomai","gloss":"to insist","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G4867","lemma":"συναθροίζω","tr":"sunathroizō","gloss":"to assemble","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G4894","lemma":"συνείδω","tr":"suneidō","gloss":"be aware","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G2678","lemma":"κατασείω","tr":"kataseiō","gloss":"to signal","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":21,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Having received permission, Paul stood on the steps and motioned to the crowd. A great hush came over the crowd, and he addressed them in Hebrew:","from":17},{"book":"MAT","chapter":18,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"See that you do not look down on any of these little ones. For I tell you that their angels in heaven always see the face of My Father in heaven.","from":15},{"book":"1JN","chapter":5,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"And this is the confidence that we have before Him: If we ask anything according to His will, He hears us.","from":12},{"book":"1JN","chapter":5,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"And if we know that He hears us in whatever we ask, we know that we already possess what we have asked of Him.","from":12},{"book":"LUK","chapter":24,"verse":41,"verseEnd":41,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"While they were still in disbelief because of their joy and amazement, He asked them, “Do you have anything here to eat?”","from":14},{"book":"ACT","chapter":12,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So Peter was kept in prison, but the church was fervently praying to God for him.","from":12},{"book":"ACT","chapter":13,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Paul stood up, motioned with his hand, and began to speak: “Men of Israel and you Gentiles who fear God, listen to me!","from":17},{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The Jews in the crowd pushed Alexander forward to explain himself, and he motioned for silence so he could make his defense to the people.","from":17}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":5},{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3},{"id":"bethany-and-friends","title":"Bethany and the Women Around Jesus","people":2}]},"18-25":{"people":[{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"herod-g2264i","name":"Herod","kind":"person","brief":"A Tetrarch","count":3,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"blastus-g0986","name":"Blastus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"barnabas-g0921g","name":"Barnabas","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mary","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"mark-g3138","name":"Mark","kind":"person","brief":"Paul's companian","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"places":[{"id":"caesarea-g2542h","name":"Caesarea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"judea-h3063n","name":"Judea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"sidon-h6721h","name":"Sidon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"tyre-h6865","name":"Tyre","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"words":[{"base":"G0937","lemma":"βασιλικός","tr":"basilikos","gloss":"royal","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"G2264","lemma":"Ἡρώδης","tr":"Hērōdēs","gloss":"Herod","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"G1096","lemma":"γίνομαι","tr":"ginomai","gloss":"to be","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668},{"base":"G4606","lemma":"Σιδώνιος","tr":"Sidōnios","gloss":"Sidonian","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G5017","lemma":"τάραχος","tr":"tarachos","gloss":"disturbance","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2250","lemma":"ἡμέρα","tr":"hēmera","gloss":"day","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":389},{"base":"G1634","lemma":"ἐκψύχω","tr":"ekpsuchō","gloss":"to expire","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G5441","lemma":"φυλακτήριος","tr":"phulaktērios","gloss":"guard","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1218","lemma":"δῆμος","tr":"dēmos","gloss":"people","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2019","lemma":"ἐπιφωνέω","tr":"epiphōneō","gloss":"to shout","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":10,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"As Peter was about to enter, Cornelius met him and fell at his feet to worship him.","from":23},{"book":"ACT","chapter":10,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"But Peter helped him up. “Stand up,” he said, “I am only a man myself.”","from":23},{"book":"PSA","chapter":115,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Not to us, O LORD, not to us, but to Your name be the glory, because of Your loving devotion, because of Your faithfulness.","from":23},{"book":"2TH","chapter":2,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"He will oppose and exalt himself above every so-called god or object of worship. So he will seat himself in the temple of God, proclaiming himself to be God.","from":23},{"book":"ACT","chapter":6,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"So the word of God continued to spread. The number of disciples in Jerusalem grew rapidly, and a great number of priests became obedient to the faith.","from":24},{"book":"ACT","chapter":12,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"And when he had realized this, he went to the house of Mary the mother of John, also called Mark, where many people had gathered together and were praying.","from":25},{"book":"ACT","chapter":14,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"But when the apostles Barnabas and Paul found out about this, they tore their clothes and rushed into the crowd, shouting,","from":23},{"book":"ACT","chapter":14,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"“Men, why are you doing this? We too are only men, human like you. We are bringing you good news that you should turn from these worthless things to the living God, who made heaven and earth and sea and everything in them.","from":23}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":4},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":4},{"id":"bethany-and-friends","title":"Bethany and the Women Around Jesus","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]}}